---
description: Open Cosmology project rules — read AGENTS.md first
alwaysApply: true
---
Before any change, read `AGENTS.md` in the repository root. It explains the architecture, the content schema, the MDX components, the writing and citation rules (every display formula is a `<Formula>` with `cite` and `at`), the MIT source and review workflow, and the next steps.

Key rules: rewrite MIT material in your own words, never copy; never reuse "All rights reserved" material; never use LibreTexts, and OpenStax only with OpenStax's written permission on file (AGENTS.md rule 10; until then no OpenStax text may be pasted, uploaded or fetched into an AI session, even with training off); recompute every number; run `npm run content:check` and `npm run build` after changes; commit only when asked.
